<title>JAPAN: Japan insurers reveal key stock index levels.</title>
<headline>Japan insurers reveal key stock index levels.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's top eight life insurance companies on Monday disclosed the levels of two key Japanese stock benchmarks, the Nikkei average and the TOPIX index, at which unrealised profits on their shareholdings would fall to zero.</p>
<p>The details are as follows:</p>
<p>			     NIKKEI		    TOPIX</p>
<p> Nippon Life	  above 12,000	    about   900</p>
<p> Dai-ichi	     14,000 - 14,500	 about 1,000</p>
<p> Meiji		  about 13,500	    about 1,000</p>
<p> Sumitomo	     17,000 - 17,500	 above 1,300</p>
<p> Yasuda		 above 16,000	    above 1,250</p>
<p> Asahi		  about 16,500	    about 1,260</p>
<p> Mitsui		 about 17,000	    about 1,280</p>
<p> Chiyoda		about 17,700	    about 1,350</p>
<p>The Nikkei closed on Monday at 20,223.82, down 261.93 or 1.28 percent, while the TOPIX closed at 1,504.92, down 4.74 or 0.31 percent.</p>
<p>The full names of the life insurers are: Meiji Life Insurance Co, Asahi Mutual Life Insurance Co, Sumitomo Life Insurance Co, Dai-Ichi Mutual Life Insurance Co, Nippon Life Insurance Co, Mitsui Mutual Life Insurance Co, Yasuda Mutual Life Insurance Co and Chiyoda Mutual Life Insurance Co.</p>
